date/time', 'NL', NULL, false, NULL, 'services received', 'the records show the service used or attended, or the cardholder present where it was given — including a payment taken in person at the place of the service, such as a taxi''s card terminal or a restaurant or venue bill; ticket or coupon details marked flown, used or redeemed; check-ins, entry scans, attendance, or log-ins and activity on the cardholder''s account. Where the merchant is an agent — it arranges a service that another business provides — arranging the booking and issuing the ticket is its own service: records of the booking made and the ticket issued bear on this argument. An airline, hotel, venue or other business selling its own service is not an agent: for it, a booking made or a ticket issued is not a service received.', 'a record the service itself made at the time of use — a boarding scan, a completed ride log, a hotel check-in, an entry or session record, a job sheet signed at the repair.', 'the records show only goods sold, delivered or collected; the service was not used — a no-show or an unused booking, which may fit the future-services argument; the merchant cancelled it; or the purchase was of cryptocurrency or an NFT whose only service was buying and sending it, which is the crypto argument.', 3, 'ALL', NULL)
